<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE UNIVERSAL ROW. One file, five archetypes.
  32-master-plan-android.md 8.1 / 5.3, 22-components.md 8.1-8.7.
  ============================================================================

  This is the single most repeated object in the product: 137 hand-inlined copies
  collapse into this file. Nothing here is optional decoration — every id below is
  a slot a caller either shows or leaves hidden, and the archetype is decided by
  WHICH ONE TRAILING SLOT is shown, never by a second layout file.

  GEOMETRY — handoff README §6 «Строка», measured off the prototype rather than
  guessed (docs/design2026/port-shots-2/43-routing.geo.json):
      [ 16 gutter ][ 40 tile r12, 22 glyph ][ 16 ][ text column ][ 12 ][ trailing ][ 16 ]
  Text origin 72 = 16 + 40 + 16 on a TILED row; 16 on a PLAIN row (5.3), which is
  what hiding @id/row_tile gives you for free — its end margin goes with it.
  Vertical padding is 10 (from @style/Widget.Departament.Row): 10 + 40 + 10 is the
  prototype's 61dp row.
  minHeight 56, height wrap_content: a two-line subtitle GROWS the row, and at font
  scale 200% every text box grows with it. There is not one fixed height in this file.

  THE TYPE IS §6's, NOT THE CARD'S. Заголовок 14sp/400 (Body) and подпись 12.5sp
  (Caption) — a row title is a LABEL the eye sweeps past, not a heading, and the
  16sp/700 this file used to carry made every settings list shout. RowBinder applies
  both roles on every bind, so the appearances below are the resting state a
  tools-preview shows and never the last word.

  THE TWO ROW SPECIES ARE DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN (5.3): a group is tiled if and only if
  its rows carry a leading glyph that DIFFERS between rows. If every row would carry
  the same glyph, the group is plain and @id/row_tile stays gone. N identical tiles
  down the left edge is the generated-settings tell, not a design.

  EVERYTHING OPTIONAL SHIPS GONE. A caller shows exactly what its archetype needs,
  so a forgotten line is a missing element and never a wrong one:

    Row.Navigation   row_title [+ row_subtitle] [+ row_value] + row_chevron
    Row.Value        row_title + row_value + row_chevron (or row_trailing_glyph to
                     cycle the value in place, which promises no screen and no dialog)
    Row.Toggle       row_title [+ row_subtitle] + row_switch
    Row.Action       row_title [+ row_subtitle] + row_icon_action OR row_action
                     AND the row itself stops being a target (see below)
    Row.Destructive  row_title in TextAppearance.App.Title.Destructive, no trailing
    Row.Fact         row_title + row_value, not clickable
    Row.Selectable   row_title [+ row_value] + row_marker, view.isActivated = true

  THE ONE SANCTIONED PAIRING (8.1): a row may carry a VALUE plus one trailing
  affordance — value + chevron (22-components 8.3) or value + state marker (the
  server row: ping plus check). The value is text, not a control. Two CONTROLS in
  the trailing slot never happens: never a chevron and a switch, never two glyphs.

  THE BINDER IS THE FRONT DOOR. ui/component/RowBinder.bind(root, title, …, trailing)
  resolves every slot below by name, shows exactly one trailing affordance, resets the
  others, and refuses at the call site to give a row two targets. Bind through it
  rather than reaching for these ids one at a time.

  WHAT CANNOT BE A LAYOUT ATTRIBUTE, AND WHY. A Material style binds at inflation, so
  three archetype deltas are applied to the inflated row instead. Each is an exact
  reproduction of a ratified style, not an invented value, and RowBinder already does
  all three for you:
    Row.Action       row.isClickable = false; row.isFocusable = false
                     row.setBackgroundResource(0)      <- @style/…Row.Action verbatim
    Row.Destructive  title.setTextAppearance(R.style.TextAppearance_App_Title_Destructive)
    accent tile      rowTile.setBackgroundResource(R.drawable.bg_tile_accent) + the
                     matching glyph tint  (D-5: one accent tile per screen, at most)
  Disabled is alpha 0.38 on the row plus isEnabled = false (R6). Pressed, focused and
  selected are already drawn by @drawable/bg_row and need no code at all.

  ACCESSIBILITY. The WHOLE ROW is the touch target — that is why the switch below is
  explicitly not clickable and not focusable (five shipped switch rows have two
  targets that can disagree). The tile is decorative and is marked as such: the title
  is the row's name. A selected row must announce it (isSelected on the a11y node),
  not only draw it.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/row"
    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Row"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:baselineAligned="false">

    <!-- TILED groups only. Gone = a plain row at the 16dp origin (5.3). The glyph is
         the caller's; the 40/12/22 geometry and the neutral fill are the style's. -->
    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/row_tile"
        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Tile"
        android:backgroundTint="?attr/colorSurfaceContainerHighest"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/tile_size"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/tile_size"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_16"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:src="@drawable/ic_settings_24dp"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- The text column. weight 1, so a long title yields to the trailing slot and a
         long value never pushes the title out of the row. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/row_text"
        android:layout_width="0dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/row_title"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="2"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body"
            tools:text="Маршрутизация" />

        <!-- A subtitle that restates its title is deleted, not written (8.1). -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/row_subtitle"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="2"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption"
            android:visibility="gone"
            tools:text="Правила для доменов и приложений"
            tools:visibility="visible" />
    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- THE TRAILING SLOT. Show exactly one control. row_value is text and may
         accompany row_chevron or row_marker; it is not a control.

         THE GAP IS NOT UNIFORM, and the difference is the handoff's, not a rounding
         error. §6: «Правый отступ 12dp только когда справа есть значение или
         переключатель» — the prototype writes it as
         `gap: (isToggle || pop || value) ? 12 : 0`. So a VALUE, a SWITCH or a BUTTON
         takes 12 from the text column, because each of those is a second thing to read
         and it needs the air. A bare GLYPH — chevron, caret, state marker — takes 4:
         it is punctuation on the row, not a second column, and 12 in front of it opens
         a gutter down the right edge of a card that has no value anywhere in it. -->

    <!-- 12dp: a value is text to be read, so it gets the full gap. -->


    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/row_value"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:gravity="end"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:text="Cloudflare"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- State marker: this item is the current selection. Not an action (8.1). The slot
         is ALWAYS reserved and selection moves its alpha, so choosing an item never
         reflows the list (22-components 18.1). -->
    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/row_marker"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/glyph_18"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/glyph_18"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_4"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:src="@drawable/ic_action_done"
        android:tint="?attr/colorPrimary"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- Tapping pushes a screen. Swap the src for the expand or cycle glyph when the
         promise changes (8.1); the size and the tone stay. -->
    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/row_chevron"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/glyph_18"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/glyph_18"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_4"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:src="@drawable/ic_chevron_right"
        android:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- Tapping changes the value in place: no screen, no dialog. The caller sets the
         glyph (the cycle affordance wants ic_unfold_more, which res/drawable does not
         carry yet), so there is no src here to be wrong. -->
    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/row_trailing_glyph"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/glyph_18"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/glyph_18"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_4"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:src="@drawable/ic_arrow_drop_down" />

    <!-- MEMBERSHIP OF A SET, not a boolean applied now (§7's «список приложений с
         чекбоксами»). 22dp box, 2dp border, radius 7, a 16dp tick that exists only
         when the box is filled — @drawable/bg_checkbox and @color/checkbox_tick do
         both halves off one state, so the row cannot draw a filled box with no tick.
         Not focusable and not clickable for the same reason the switch is not: the
         WHOLE row is the target. -->
    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/row_check_box"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/checkbox_size"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/checkbox_size"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
        android:background="@drawable/bg_checkbox"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:padding="@dimen/space_2"
        android:scaleType="fitCenter"
        android:src="@drawable/ic_action_done"
        android:tint="@color/checkbox_tick"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- The row owns the toggle; the switch is decoration that reports state. -->
    <com.google.android.material.materialswitch.MaterialSwitch
        android:id="@+id/row_switch"
        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Switch"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
        android:clickable="false"
        android:focusable="false"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- Row.Action's in-place action. When this is shown the ROW is not a target:
         two targets doing different things is the layout_subscription_meta_bar
         mistake. android:contentDescription is MANDATORY and states the ACTION.

         ITS END MARGIN IS NOT ZERO AT RUNTIME, and this is the one slot in the file
         where that is true. The glyphs above are 18dp ImageViews whose box sits on
         the row's 16dp end padding; this is a 48dp touch minimum with a 22dp icon
         centred in it, so 13dp of the box is air on the trailing side and the ink
         lands 10 to 16dp further in than a chevron's — «они улетели куда-то влево».
         RowBinder.alignInkToGutter pulls the box back per glyph on every bind (the
         two glyphs that reach this slot differ by 6.4dp between themselves), which
         is why the correction is not written here. The 48dp target keeps all 48. -->
    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
        android:id="@+id/row_icon_action"
        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Icon"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
        android:visibility="gone"
        app:icon="@drawable/ic_copy"
        tools:ignore="ContentDescription"
        tools:visibility="visible" />

    <!-- The other half of Row.Action: a Tertiary button, and this row is the ONLY place
         in the product a Tertiary is allowed to live inside a row («Привязать Telegram»
         -> «Привязать»). The row is inert whenever this is showing. -->
    <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
        android:id="@+id/row_action"
        style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
        android:visibility="gone"
        tools:text="Привязать"
        tools:visibility="visible" />
</LinearLayout>
